Subject: [PATCH 163/163] GreatDANE: commit the StaticPrefs libpref edits; wire
 the overlay hook

Round-3 conditions (C1 and the LOW note).

Commit the libpref edits into the series: StaticPrefList.yaml gets
greatdane.node.lazy (RelaxedAtomicBool, false) and
greatdane.node.lazyTimeoutSec (RelaxedAtomicInt32, 10), and moz.build
pref_groups gets "greatdane". These are exactly what the overlay
patches apply (yaml cfd51e265d70, moz.build d41cd906de04 from
ee74e0dce6aa / 79b7b9fdffb5), so a tree built from the series carries
them and its HEAD tree is the tree that is built.

Add greatdane/tools/apply-dane-series.sh as the build entry point: it
git am's patches/series, then runs apply-greatdane-overlay.sh --check
(fail closed, no writes) and the hook, and commits any change to the
two libpref paths. It refuses a dirty tree and any other hook change.
--hook-only runs just the hook step, for pipelines that apply the
series themselves, after their last product commit and before
clobber / configure. greatdane/tools/OVERLAY-HOOK.md says where the
pinned Linux pipeline gets the call at its next re-pin.

LOW: --check on an already-applied tree now runs the exact-count and
type checks before reporting OK, so a duplicated entry fails. Escape
the dots in those patterns.

Tests: test_overlay_hook.py (synthetic libpref trees, no network)
covers the hook wiring, fail-closed cases, the commit, and --check on
a duplicated tree. test_static_prefs_patch.py has no default Firefox
tree path any more; set GREATDANE_FIREFOX_SRC.

No mach.
